Appendix H — Sabatier Reactor Kinetics Data

H.1 Catalyst and Conditions

The Sabatier reaction kinetics in the thesis are based on the 0.5 % Ru/γ‑Al₂O₃ catalyst studied by Lunde & Kester (1973, Journal of Catalysis). Experimental conditions: 1 atm total pressure, H₂:CO₂ feed ratios 1.9–3.9, temperatures 477–633 K (400–680 °F), 4.15 cm³ isothermal reactor, 62 experimental runs covering 0–85 % conversion.

H.2 Kinetic Parameters

NASA Technical Memorandum (1975) confirms that the reaction fits a power‑function rate law over 421–800 K, with activation energies determined from Arrhenius plots of differential rate data. The Langmuir‑Hinshelwood form with E_a \approx 100 kJ mol⁻¹ and equilibrium constant K_p \approx 10^{10} at 300 °C is used in the thesis specification.

