Appendix L — Polynomial Chaos Expansion Validation

The core methodology for uncertainty quantification in this thesis is sparse polynomial chaos expansion (PCE) as applied to Mars life support system modelling. Makrygiorgos, Georgakis & Mesbah (2020, IFAC‑PapersOnLine) demonstrated that sparse polynomial chaos‑Kriging (PCK) achieves a 100‑fold computational speed‑up in estimating the probability distribution of the minimum equivalent system mass for a Mars crop cultivation model with 86 uncertain parameters.

Key findings from this benchmark:

· PCK surrogate accurately reproduces the full model output distribution.
· 100× computational gain vs. Monte‑Carlo for equivalent accuracy.
· Global sensitivity analysis identifies which crop‑growth and equipment‑operation parameters dominate mission‑outcome variability.
· The methodology is directly transferable to the broader habitat‑scale UQ specified in the thesis.

