Appendix N — MELiSSA Pilot Plant Benchmarks

The MELiSSA (Micro‑Ecological Life Support System Alternative) pilot plant at the University of Barcelona has operated continuously since 2009, integrating photobioreactors, microbial compartments, and a higher‑plant chamber connected to an animal compartment (rats). Key design features relevant to the thesis specification:

· Stoichiometric mass‑balance tracking of C, H, O, N, S, P across all compartments.
· Compartmentalised closed‑loop architecture with six biological compartments.
· Demonstrated long‑term stable operation (over 10 years).
· The mass‑balance Simulink model validates the feasibility of stoichiometric‑matrix‑based conservation enforcement at the compartment level — the thesis extends this principle to the full habitat level.

